A||||5||dizmon_85GT||Different headlight woes, another PROBLEM!!||||8||
Z||000000||dizmon_85GT||08-30-2001||02:42 PM||||I dismantled my motor again to give it a good cleaning and lube and now when I connect the single blue wire which normally brings the light down, it now wants to bring it up!!!!  What have I done wrong????? HELP!!!!!!||||reg||8
Z||000001||JetroGT||08-30-2001||04:17 PM||||If it's an 84-86 you can try to adjust it. With it all the way down, turn the top clock wise a turn or two, then try it. It worked for my lights.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Rodney||08-30-2001||05:22 PM||||Magnet in backwards. (upside down??)||||reg||1
Z||000003||dizmon_85GT||08-30-2001||06:06 PM||||Rodney, <BR>  I did pull the motor shaft out to clean it. I did not take the magnet off the shaft.  Do you mean turn the magnet around the shaft (180 deg. around to the other side) so the side that is now facing up is down?  There is a white dot on the magnet.  Does it need to be up or down when you pull the cover off?<BR>Thanks for your responce.||||reg||11
Z||000004||Rodrv6||08-30-2001||09:54 PM||||I would take it back apart and rotate that magnet 180 degrees.  I don't recall which way the white dot should face, but I had the same problem on my 84 a number of years ago and that fixed it.<P>------------------<BR>Rod Schneider, Woodstock, Ga.  84 SE, 330,000 miles and counting, 88 GT, not nearly as many miles :)||||reg||1
Z||000005||dizmon_85GT||09-27-2001||02:47 PM||||Rodney,<P>   I finally got around to working on the headlight issue and disassembled the motor.  Took your advive about the magnet in backwards and rotated it 180 deg. around the shaft and it works like a charm!!! Thanks a million.  It was driving me crazy!!!<P>BTW, when I took the cover off and rotated the magnet body, the white dot is now  facing up.||||reg||10
